---
import "../styles/style.css";
import "../styles/about.css";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <title>fabbeyond.dev - About</title>
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.0/css/all.min.css"
    />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Navbar />
    <div class="nav-bar-divider"></div>

    <main>
      <div class="about-content">
        <p class="about-title">ABOUT</p>

        <p class="about-intro">
          My name is Fabian, or Fab for short, and I'm a 16 yr. old programmer
          from Austria.
        </p>
        <p class="about-intro">
          Currently, while working on miscellaneous projects, I'm studing Game
          Design at{" "}
          <a href="https://www.spengergasse.at" target="_blank">
            HTL Spengergasse
          </a>{" "}
          in Vienna.
        </p>

        <p>
          I had my first experience with coding around the age of 8. My dad
          introduced me to an app called{" "}
          <a href="https://www.scratchjr.org/">"Scratch Jr."</a> which I quickly
          outgrew and I switched over to the full version{" "}
          <a href="https://scratch.mit.edu/">Scratch</a>. This was my main
          programming language for a few years until I tried out Python. Due to
          my extensive use of Scratch I quickly grasped how written coding works
          and started making little projects like Quizzes, small drawings with
          the Turtle library and simple UIs with tkinter. Around that time I
          attended lots of coding summer camps for Scratch, Python and Unity. I
          was so advanced at that point that I even got to teach the other
          attending kids something.
        </p>

        <p>
          Then I got really interested in Game Development and tried out Unity &
          C#, which I still use to make games. My first finished and released
          game,{" "}
          <a href="https://fabbeyond.itch.io/balanced-load">"Balanced Load"</a>,
          was made for the{" "}
          <a href="https://itch.io/jam/gmtk-2024">GTMK 2024 Game Jam</a>. Both
          other released games,{" "}
          <a href="https://fabbeyond.itch.io/fortuna">"Fortuna"</a> &{" "}
          <a href="https://fabbeyond.itch.io/ohcrab">"Oh, Crab!"</a>, were made
          for the internal Spengergasse Game Jams, 2025 & 2026 respectfully.
          "Fortuna" was made when I was in first grade and actually won the Jam
          making me and my team the first ever first-graders to win the Game
          Jam.
        </p>
        <p>
          During the same time I also got interested in Modding. I started
          simple by making small mods for{" "}
          <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/2236070/Peaks_of_Yore/">
            "Peaks of Yore"
          </a>
          , a 3D physics-based climbing game. Once I got more comfortable
          modding I made slightly bigger and mroe complex mods for{" "}
          <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/1030300/Hollow_Knight_Silksong/">
            "Silksong"
          </a>{" "}
          and{" "}
          <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/322170/Geometry_Dash/">
            "Geometry Dash"
          </a>
          . My experience with Unity helped tremendously with Modding Unity
          games and made it way easier to get started. Over the course of 1.5
          years all my mods reached around 60 thousand downloads, my most
          popular one{" "}
          <a href="https://geode-sdk.org/mods/fabbeyond.layouttools">
            "Layout Tools"
          </a>
          , for Geometry Dash, having amassed over 30k downloads.
        </p>

        <p>
          Around early 2026 I became interested in self hosting servers for
          various purposes like Discord bots, Minecraft servers, Websites, etc.
          I used my old PC as a home server which I run said things on. This
          means I have a decent understanding of Linux and servers as a whole.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <div class="nav-bar-divider"></div>
  </body>

  <Footer />
</html>
